From 02b1f3f3da87194b105eaccbf46744a5e2eeb849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:39:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] VPVulkan: GPU-written indirect arguments read on the GPU
 (metal2 fix-up kernel: count, multiview, clamp), CPU-path clamps, per-encoder
 hang diagnostics, command queue recovery

Alyx (build 12) hung the GPU on its first scene frame: indirect draw arguments
written by the GPU were read on the CPU at submit (stale/garbage counts), then
Metal ignored every later submission.
